- Windows MDM hosts are now sent a per-device, single-use enroll secret instead of the shared global enroll secret when `auth.use_one_time_enroll_secrets` is enabled. The secret is minted per MDM enrollment and expanded when the command is delivered, so it is no longer stored in plaintext in the MDM command queue or returned by the MDM command results API.
- Added a Fleet-managed "Fleet enroll secret" Windows configuration profile that delivers the one-time enroll secret to the host's registry. Resending it is how an administrator recovers a Windows host whose enroll secret was already used, and only an administrator can resend it.
- A Windows host that enrolls with a one-time enroll secret is now linked to the MDM enrollment that secret was minted for, instead of the enrollment being matched from a hardware serial reported by the device.
- The Windows installer no longer writes the enroll secret into verbose MSI logs. Fleet MDM passes the secret on the msiexec command line, where `/l*v` previously recorded it in cleartext six times per install.
